Configure it in the table config under tableIndexConfig.

Use starTreeIndexConfigs for explicit control.

Or set enableDefaultStarTree: true for Pinot's default configuration.

New segments get the index. Existing segments do not.

A minimal config looks like this:

{
  "tableIndexConfig": {
    "starTreeIndexConfigs": [
      {
        "dimensionsSplitOrder": ["Country", "Browser", "Locale"],
        "skipStarNodeCreationForDimensions": [],
        "functionColumnPairs": ["SUM__Impressions"],
        "maxLeafRecords": 1
      }
    ]
  }
}

You can also use aggregationConfigs instead of functionColumnPairs:

"aggregationConfigs": [
  {
    "columnName": "Impressions",
    "aggregationFunction": "SUM",
    "compressionCodec": "LZ4"
  }
]

Key rules:
- Put all filter, group-by, and aggregation columns used by matching queries into dimensionsSplitOrder.
- Star-tree dimension columns must be dictionary-encoded.
- maxLeafRecords defaults to 10000.
- skipStarNodeCreationForDimensions is optional.
- enableDefaultStarTree builds a default index from: all dictionary-encoded single-value dimensions with cardinality <= 10000, dictionary-encoded time/date-time columns, COUNT(*) and SUM for numeric metrics.

Sources: Style Guide, Star-Tree Index, Monitoring Metrics, Troubleshooting, Use S3 as Deep Storage for Pinot, Ingestion FAQ, Components, Configure Indexes, Overview, Trino

